{title: Rock of Ages}
{artist: Augustus Toplady & Thomas Hastings}
{key: Bb}
{time: 6/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[Bb]Rock of Ages, [F]cleft for [Bb]me, [Eb]let me [Bb]hide my[F]self in [Bb]thee;
let the water [F]and the [Bb]blood, [Eb]from thy [Bb]wounded [F]side which [Bb]flowed,
[F]be of sin the [Bb]double cure: [Eb]save from [Bb]wrath and [F]make me [Bb]pure.

Verse 2
[Bb]Not the labor [F]of my [Bb]hands [Eb]Can [Bb]fulfill Thy law's [Bb]demands;
Could my zeal [F]no respite [Bb]know, [Eb]Could [Bb]my [F]tears forever [Bb]flow,
[F]All for sin could [Bb]not atone; [Eb]Thou [Bb]must save, [F]and Thou [Bb]alone.

Verse 3
[Bb]Nothing in my [F]hand I [Bb]bring, [Eb]Simply to [Bb]the cross I [Bb]cling;
Naked, come to [F]Thee for [Bb]dress; [Eb]Helpless look [Bb]to [F]Thee for [Bb]grace;
[F]Foul, I to the [Bb]fountain fly; [Eb]Wash [Bb]me, Savior, [F]or I [Bb]die.

Verse 4
[Bb]While I draw [F]this fleeting [Bb]breath, [Eb]When mine [Bb]eyes shall close [Bb]in
death, When I [F]soar to [Bb]worlds [Eb]unknown, See [Bb]Thee [F]on Thy [Bb]judgment
[F]throne, Rock of Ages, [Bb]cleft for [Eb]me, Let [Bb]me hide [F]myself in [Bb]Thee.
